  "releaseNotes": "10.3.4\n\n* Fixed: DataExtensions.GetDataModelParameters read every JSON number as a double, so an integer\n  from 2^53 (9007199254740992) on lost its last digits: 9007199254740993 became 9007199254740992.\n  Such an integer, of either sign, is now a long, with every digit, up to the largest long. Every other number is\n  still a double. A caller that casts such a value to double must convert it instead\n  (Convert.ToDouble).\n\nUpgrading from an earlier version? 10.3.3 changed how Fill and FillDate treat a value that holds a\nplaceholder, 10.3.1 what IOExtensions.UnifyPathSeperator does with a leading // or \\\\ on Windows,\nand 10.3.0 how Com.H.Shell and Com.H.Pdf behave. The notes of 10.3.0 to 10.3.3 list every change:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.3#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.2#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.1#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.0#releasenotes-body-tab",
